      "evidence": "The sentence says a nonzero class whose support reaches the boundary “creates a jump.” On Ω=(0,1), u(x)=x(1−x) is nonzero and its support closure [0,1] meets the boundary, but its zero extension has weak derivative (1−2x)1_(0,1): both endpoint values vanish, so there are no Dirac terms, and the extension lies in W^{1,p}(R) for every 1≤p≤∞.",
